# Altair design system

## Reuse tokens — do not invent chrome

Prefer existing Altair materials and semantic roles in `shared/design-system/foundation/altair-tokens.ts` (`bg-altair-*`, `text-altair-*`, `border-altair-*`, success/warning/danger/information). Compose from design-system components (`EmptyState`, `MetricCard`, `StatusPill`, shell primitives) before adding parallel cards, colors, or radii.

Do not hardcode new hex values or introduce a second token vocabulary for a page.

## Surface registers (do not mix)

**Mission Control v2 light paper** — Dashboard, Customers, Customer Profile, hubs, Settings:

- Tokens: `shared/design-system/components/mc-surface.ts`
- Classes: `altairMcCardClass`, `altairMcTileClass`, `altairMcListClass`, `altairMcMetricLabelClass`, `altairMcMetricValueClass`, etc.
- Sharp corners (`rounded-none`); warm hairline `border-[var(--north-star-border)]` (`#838f68`).
- Two-tone canvas: `--north-star-header-strip` vs `--north-star-content-well` (shell + page header bands).
- Surfaces use `--surface-section` / `--surface-tile` / `--surface-card` on the olive content well.

**Reports dark elevated** — Reports (and Dispatch board, deliberate exception):

- Tokens: `shared/design-system/components/report-surface.ts`
- Classes: `altairReportCardClass`, `altairReportTileClass`, `altairReportMetric*Class`, range/action chrome.
- Background is Graphite (`bg-altair-graphite`) — do not invent a parallel dark hex.
- Dispatch additionally uses a dark Ink canvas wrapper and saturated priority chip fills for Gantt readability; keep that exception scoped to `/dispatch`.

**Reports icon chips only** — `shared/design-system/components/report-icon-tints.ts`:

- Categorical tints (`reportIconTintClass` / `reportIconChipClassName`) are scoped to icon-chip backgrounds.
- Never use those hues for text, trends, borders, or status meaning.
- Never mix categorical chip tints with semantic success / warning / danger roles. Trends still use semantic success/danger.

## Data honesty

Never fabricate metrics, percentages, comparisons, or “on pace” copy. Every number must trace to a real query field, rollup, or typed helper. If the data is missing:

1. Use an honest empty / em-dash state (`EmptyState`, `"—"`, permission-gated copy), or
2. Cut the element entirely.

Do not invent sample deltas, fake CLV, ratings, or forecast figures to fill a layout. See `docs/altair-feature-gaps.md` before building anything on that list.

## Money collected = payment ledger

“Money collected”, “Total Spent”, “lifetime revenue” (payment total), and similar collected figures are always the sum of `invoice_payments` amounts (payment ledger) — e.g. `sumCollectedRevenue` in `shared/lib/reports/report-metrics.ts`.

Never use a cached invoice field such as `amount_paid` / `amountPaid` as the collected-revenue source of truth for dashboards, reports, or customer profile stats.

## Build workflow

- Work in small, verified passes (layout → audit real data → wire → verify).
- Audit live data shapes and permissions before wiring UI.
- When scope is ambiguous, ask — do not guess product meaning or invent metrics.
- Track redesign status in `docs/altair-build-roadmap.md`.
